<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  Configurations GUI definition - standard format (single root, well-formed).
  Version notes: 3.1.4 parameters are numbered from 1 (the first field of a group, e.g. Radio status, no longer sorts last);
  3.1.3 standard-MIB fallbacks (IP, mask, gateway, MTU); 3.1.2 declared <DeviceType>; 3.1.1 Ethernet speed enum.

  Same <parameter> blocks as the client file "Configurations_GUI 3.xml"; every <oid> is the table COLUMN OID, as
  in the MIB.  Nothing here contains device values or per-radio OIDs:

    <Identity>      the product (DefinitionId, vendor, model) and how a device is recognised (sysObjectID prefix)
    <InstanceMaps>  how a table's row index maps to a component.  A section (or a parameter) with
                    instances="radio" is expanded by the NMS into one group per row: OID = column OID + "." + row
                    (+ the map's suffix), shown as Wireless / Radio 1 / Properties.
    sections without instances="..." are read as they are (scalars, e.g. IP configuration).
    <fallback source="..."/> names a STANDARD-MIB source (IP-MIB / IF-MIB) used only when the vendor OID answers with a
                    placeholder: ip.address, ip.netmask, ip.gateway, mgmt.mtu — single GETs only, never a table walk.

  Row numbers verified on UBR655 units (fw 1.0.0.161): wirelessTable / wirelessStatsTable 1 = 2.4 GHz, 2 = Radio 1,
  3 = Radio 2; link-profile (DDRS/ATPC, index radio.1) and DCS tables 2 = Radio 1, 3 = Radio 2; VLAN 1 / 2 = Radio 1 / 2;
  Ethernet 1 / 2 = eth0 / eth1; assocTable rows are radio.station.
-->
